From 88b1a284d3a68bdaa24c6a3562b8fb7f6dbc77e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Shevlyakov <igor@tachyum.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:52:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] match.pd: Use ssizetype masks when merging VEC_PERMs
 [PR128080]

The patterns merging two VEC_PERM_EXPRs give the new selector the
element type of the outer permute's mask.  The new selector indexes two
vectors of N elements, so its elements range over 0 .. 2N-1, and with
256 or more byte elements an 8-bit mask element cannot hold them:
build_int_cst truncates the index and the merged permute reads the
wrong input.  For example

  c = VEC_PERM_EXPR <b, b, { 255, 254, ..., 0 }>;
  d = VEC_PERM_EXPR <x, c, { 0, -1, ... }>;

was merged to VEC_PERM_EXPR <x, x, { 0, 0, ... }>, the index 256 of
b[0] having become 0.

A constant permute mask is not tied to the element type of the vectors
it permutes, so build the new one with ssizetype elements, as the
vectorizer and forwprop do, in all three patterns.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5

	PR tree-optimization/128080

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* match.pd (vec_perm (vec_perm) merges): Give the new mask
	ssizetype elements.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c: New test.
	* gcc.dg/torture/pr128080-2.c: New test.

Signed-off-by: Igor Shevlyakov <igor@tachyum.com>
(cherry picked from commit f4c8d2716469a587a97f8a325d032d539f00e2f0)
